{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q422755","formula":"C₂HCl₃O","hill":"C2HCl3O","elements":["H","C","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":1.0,"O":1.0,"Cl":3.0},"names":{"en":"Chloral","ru":"Хлораль"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chloral, also known as trichloroacetaldehyde or trichloroethanal, is the organic compound with the formula Cl3CCHO. This aldehyde is a colourless liquid that is soluble in a wide range of solvents. It reacts with water to form chloral hydrate, a once widely used sedative and hypnotic substance.","ru":"Хлораль (трихлорацетальдегид, трихлоруксусный альдегид) — органическое соединение, принадлежащее к классу альдегидов, соответствующее трихлоруксусной кислоте; бесцветная жидкость со специфическим резким запахом, растворим в органических растворителях и нерастворим в воде. Впервые получен в 1832 г. Юстусом Либихом при хлорировании этанола."},"fame":35,"pubchemCid":6407,"mass":147.38,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=O)C(Cl)(Cl)Cl","inchikey":"HFFLGKNGCAIQMO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2,2,2-trichloroacetaldehyde","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6407","atoms":7,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.131,"y":-0.006,"z":1.778,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.246,"y":1.46,"z":-0.477,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.246,"y":-1.457,"z":-0.487,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.049,"y":0.0,"z":-0.147,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.376,"y":0.0,"z":0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":0.949,"y":0.002,"z":-0.692,"el":"C"},{"x":0.894,"y":0.006,"z":-1.796,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[1,4,1],[2,4,1],[3,5,2],[4,5,1],[5,6,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422755","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chloral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A5%D0%